# DHI-11 V6 — Controlled comparison design

**DESIGN ONLY. No samples prepared, no sensory data, no physical or skin-use authority.** Obtain product/SDS/stock and safety qualification before any bench or participant work. See [master formula](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_Orris_Led_30mL_20pct.md) and [pour card](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/formulas/DHI-11_V6_Complexity_First_30mL_POUR_CARD.md).

## Question and protected nucleus

Does adding cold/root contrast and warm/cream pressure together make the iris more legible and engaging than either module alone, without gourmand, violet, camphor or woody-musk takeover? This is not a test that assumes the most complex arm wins.

Keep Orris Liquid, AIMI, Alpha Irone and Alpha Ionone at the exact V6 stock identities and planned amounts in every arm. All non-test rows are also fixed. The common core is the V6 table excluding the eight distinct rows in the two modules below.

| Module | Stock rows and full-reference transfers | Subtotal |
|---|---|---:|
| Cold/root | Beta Ionone 20 µL; Dihydro Beta Ionone 60 µL; Orivone 10 µL; Carrot Seed EO 10 µL | 100 µL |
| Warm/cream | Ebanol 30 µL; Sandalore 50 µL; Isobutavan 50 µL; Delta Decalactone 10 µL | 140 µL |

These are operational module names, not experimentally established temperature sensations. Every test-module row is neat/as supplied; no hidden stock carrier is changed inside these modules.

## Four equal-volume arms

| Arm key — conceal from evaluator | Common core | Cold/root | Warm/cream | Explicit Ethanol 96% balancing transfer | Final Ethanol 96% addition |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| A00 | 5760 µL | 0 µL | 0 µL | 240 µL | 24,000 µL |
| B10 | 5760 µL | 100 µL | 0 µL | 140 µL | 24,000 µL |
| C01 | 5760 µL | 0 µL | 140 µL | 100 µL | 24,000 µL |
| D11 | 5760 µL | 100 µL | 140 µL | 0 µL | 24,000 µL |

Each core-plus-variable portion totals 6,000 µL and each nominal finished arm totals 30,000 µL. **These are raw-volume controlled, not exact active-mass or solvent-matrix matched.** Replacing omitted neat odorants with ethanol changes odorant loading and solvent matrix. That balancing intervention is explicit. Neither inert DPG nor Benzyl Benzoate can be assumed perceptually/physically neutral. Do not attribute every difference to an abstract “layer” or claim isolated receptor synergy.

## Smaller samples without sub-10 µL stock transfers

For a later qualified nominal 3 mL sample, do not divide the eight stock additions directly.

1. Prepare the full-reference 5,760 µL common core from V6's other 25 rows, in their basket order; record delivered masses and confirm homogeneity.
2. Prepare a separate 240 µL variable module for each arm using the full transfers shown above, including its explicit balancing ethanol. Each individual selected stock transfer is at least 10 µL.
3. For each sample, combine 576 µL common core, 24 µL of its homogeneous variable module and 2,400 µL Ethanol 96%. Sum: 3,000 µL nominal.
4. Prepare a second independent set, not merely a relabelled aliquot, to inspect preparation repeatability. Record lot, date, temperature, delivered mass, solvent loss and appearance. No maturation interval is claimed optimal by this design.

The prescribed common-core batch can support multiple samples; leftover volume is not authority to combine or rework arms. No heating or unqualified solid/liquid substitution is introduced.

## Blinding, observations and decisions

A separate preparer assigns nonsemantic random labels and keeps the arm key sealed until ratings are recorded. The A/B/C/D keys printed here are explanatory labels, not successful blinding. Balance presentation order across repeat sessions; use the same substrate, applied amount and interval since application. Record unprompted descriptions before layer prompts.

Record intensity, iris recognizability, richness/coherence, pleasure, harshness, powder/root balance, cream/dry-grain coexistence and any violet/fruit/camphor/wood takeover separately. Use anchored 0–10 ratings with identical wording across arms. Ratings are exploratory repeated observations, not a powered population study or an absolute-hedonism index.

For a qualified non-skin blotter/fabric setup, observe at 5, 30, 120 and 240 minutes and at 0.1, 0.5, 1 and 2 m. Record measured airflow/direction, ventilation, temperature, humidity, substrate and loading. Standardize distance and observer position; do not call a room plume an outdoor result. Use clean-air intervals and stop with irritation; no intentional high-concentration inhalation. OAV predictions cannot replace these receiver observations.

For each outcome, inspect the factorial interaction D11 − B10 − C01 + A00 alongside individual arm scores. In this solvent-balanced exploratory design, this is a descriptive interaction contrast, not proof of molecular synergy. Prefer the richer arm only if iris identity and coherence remain acceptable and its useful benefit recurs; no improvement or a drift penalty is a valid rejection.

## Follow-up tests that preserve learning

After the cold/warm comparison, test each added material and its strongest alternative with the protected nucleus. A sub-threshold model result alone cannot choose retention, and a null sensory test should not be relabelled hidden complexity.

Pairwise musk tests: Ambrettolide × EB; Ambrettolide × Romandolide; EB × Romandolide. For each, compare both, each alone and neither, keeping other assigned jobs fixed and documenting every balance carrier. Compare Habanolide only in the late-contour role as a separate arm after stock/safety qualification. Repeatability of loss, preservation of iris and a distinct role are required; no three-musk preference is assumed.

Compare richer V6 against a compressed candidate only after the module losses are understood. The compressed arm is not automatically A00, and must have its own source-function ledger. Rejection of a row must preserve its useful function question or explicitly reject it with evidence.

## What the system may learn

Save physical preparation metadata, blinded raw ratings, controls, exclusions and reproducibility limitations before interpreting outcomes. Current project knowledge contains identity gaps, model limits, source provenance and testable hypotheses; there are no sensory observations or model-weight updates. Papers support methods, not certified pleasure of this candidate.

Scientific rationale and verified source links are in [the September 6 research report](C:/Users/ASUS/.codex/worktrees/c4d5/perfume-chem/docs/research/DHI2011_COMPLEXITY_FIRST_OPEN_SPACE_RESEARCH_20260906.md). DHP protocol acceptance remains HOLD because the executable donor-independence gate is not available in this checkout.
